Have you tried Robert Cook's tiles? I find them a
nice compromise, with the objects, effects, and
dungeon layout graphical, and the monsters
"decorated text characters". Plus, the tiles are
twice as high as wide, so you get a better fit of
tiles to standard screen dimensions today. If the
10x20 set makes you squint, there's a pixel
replicated 20x40 set as well.

http://www.olywa.net/cook/nhack.htm

Quantum valeat.

xanthian.

I'm also slowly making a 15x30 version, but it's
a very low priority project, as each tile needs to
be done pretty much "from scratch" but honoring
Robert's intent, and so the set won't be done any
time soon.  The half-baked version I have now is the
one I use myself to play, done or not. [The "undone"
other tiles are scaled from the 20x40 set, which
doesn't work all that well (stuff blurs across the
tile boundaries, e.g., and the tiles internally
aren't all that crisp), but suffices for play if one
isn't too fussy.]




